# Production Executive, Audio / Video / Photography Production

Job ID: 10481119 | Amazon Digital UK Limited

## Description

We are seeking a seasoned production professional to aid in Amazon MGM Studio's International Originals content creation. The successful candidate will possess the ability to complete high volumes of complex tasks and projects quickly; react with appropriate urgency to situations and events that require quick response or turnaround; and efficiently and creatively help solve difficult or complex problems that affect people within the business.

This position will report to the Head of Production and Post, International Originals UK & EUX and will be assigned a specific set of show projects within the organization. The candidate will also have great attention to detail and organization skills, as well as the ability to switch gears at a moment's notice. A high level of integrity and discretion in handling confidential information and professionalism in dealing with senior professionals inside and outside the company is key. The role requires versatility in supporting a diverse portfolio of projects with a focus on unscripted series, but ranging from movies and series rather than a single genre. The candidate will be comfortable working across various formats and production types to support Amazon MGM's broad content offering.

Key job responsibilities
- Support multiple projects in development and production, through delivery and launch;
- Coordinate with show producers, production teams and creative executives in budget and production meetings;
- Works with internal departments and production companies on production safety, security, insurance, child labour, immigration, visa, travel, and tax issues;
- Is on-set when necessary to evaluate work-flow, budgets and potential problems both domestically and abroad (as needed);
- Analyse budgets and cost reports;
- Works with post-production to insure delivery of all required assets;
- Coordination with other internal departments such as creative, marketing, press, business affairs, legal, finance, and tax.


Key job responsibilities
- Extensive experience as a producer/ line producer/ production executive
- Strong knowledge and experience in all forms of productions across all budget levels;
- High level of competency with budgeting, scheduling, and cost reports;
- On-set problem solving ability.

## Basic Qualifications

- Experience with budgeting, scheduling and cost reports
- Experience in budgeting, scheduling and technical workflows
- Experience working as a producer, production executive, or a similar role

## Preferred Qualifications

- International production experience desirable;
- Strong knowledge in unscripted, scripted or movies production;
- Experience with above-the-line and below-the-line unions and guilds;
- Working knowledge of location specific production guidelines and procedures;
- Wide array of industry contacts;
- Experience with asset delivery;
- Experience with a variety of digital and cloud media workflows and post production;
- High attention to detail;
- Detailed planning, time management, and organisational skills;
- Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills;
- Positive can-do attitude with strong initiative and follow through;
- Great judgment and common sense;
- Ability to work in a rapidly changing environment;
- Creative problem-solver;
- High levels of integrity and discretion in handling confidential information;
- Awareness of producers, production companies, agents, and other industry players;
- Tech-savvy: familiar with online video environment.

Amazon is an equal opportunities employer. We believe passionately that employing a diverse workforce is central to our success. We make recruiting decisions based on your experience and skills. We value your passion to discover, invent, simplify and build. Protecting your privacy and the security of your data is a longstanding top priority for Amazon. Please consult our Privacy Notice to know more about how we collect, use and transfer the personal data of our candidates.

